<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI-REQDOC-PATHEQUIV-PRIVATE>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI-REQDOC-PATHEQUIV-PRIVATE" ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-27T22:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-Legacy ;
  triage:title "Path-equivalence rule documentation generalizes only to loopback and self-IP, silent on third-party private-range addresses" ;
  triage:description "Code audit confirmed PostWriteRouter::dispatch (crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/peer_delivery_router.rs) branches only on host-present-vs-empty with zero IP-class inspection, fully satisfying the intent: 'when sending to 127.0.0.1, 192.168.x.x, or any other loopback/private-range IP, that send must follow the exact same code path as sending to any other IP or hostname — no special-casing, no exceptions.' All is_loopback() call sites are legitimate listener-accept/self-publish integrity gates, not send-routing decisions. However, requirements and ADR documents illustrate this path-equivalence rule only with localhost, 127.0.0.1, or 'the daemon's own advertised/bound IP address' — none explicitly generalize to arbitrary private-range IPs addressing a *different* host (e.g., 192.168.x.x pointing at another daemon on the LAN). Specific instances: (1) ADR-035 Decision paragraph 1 states 'every validated present destination host selects the HTTPS transport adapter, including localhost and this daemon's advertised or bound IP address' — broad clause but narrow illustrative list. (2) ADR-035 Decision paragraph 3: 'localhost and a daemon's own advertised address are ordinary host values' — names only the familiar cases. (3) docs/requirements.md REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-002C: 'Same-host proof must use the ordinary remote-host contract' — scoped to same-host only, silent on third-party private-range. (4) docs/atm-core/requirements.md AI.23 constraint names the function chain (ApiRouter::route → DaemonRequestDispatcher::route_write → MessageWriter::write → PostWriteRouter::dispatch) but without the full generalization statement. (5) ADR-035 Prohibitions clause ('No socket-family or socket-address inference') is the strongest generic rule, but other docs don't reference it as canonical. Consequence: ambiguity about whether path-equivalence is guaranteed for 192.168.x.x → arbitrary-peer-daemon or only for localhost/self-IP. This is a clarity gap; code is already compliant by construction." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "documentation-only" ;
  triage:category "requirements-doc" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-27T22:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI-REQDOC-PATHEQUIV-PRIVATE/adr-035-decision-narrowing> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI-REQDOC-PATHEQUIV-PRIVATE/req-core-transport-002c-scoping> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI-REQDOC-PATHEQUIV-PRIVATE/ai23-missing-generalization> ;
  triage:searchedLocations "docs/requirements.md | docs/atm-core/requirements.md | docs/adr/ADR-031.md | docs/adr/ADR-033.md | docs/adr/ADR-034.md | docs/adr/ADR-035.md | docs/sprint-ai-22.md" ;
  triage:searchPatterns "localhost | 127.0.0.1 | advertised address | bound IP | path-equivalence | same-host | private.*range" ;
  triage:relatedCodeFiles "crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/peer_delivery_router.rs" ;
  triage:notes "Code is fully compliant; this is a documentation clarification issue. Recommend: (1) generalize REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-002 / 002C in docs/requirements.md and docs/atm-core/requirements.md to explicitly state that path-equivalence applies to every destination host regardless of IP class (loopback, private-range, or public), not just loopback/self-IP examples. (2) Add canonical reference in both docs to ADR-035 Prohibitions clause ('No socket-family or socket-address inference') and the AI.23 named function chain as the enforceable definition other docs should cite rather than restate loosely. Non-critical for code function but necessary for doc completeness and architect confidence." .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI-REQDOC-PATHEQUIV-PRIVATE/adr-035-decision-narrowing>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "docs/adr/ADR-035.md" ;
  triage:description "ADR-035 Decision paragraphs 1 and 3 state path-equivalence rule but only illustrate with localhost and daemon's own advertised/bound IP address, not arbitrary private-range addressing third-party hosts" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:closed false .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI-REQDOC-PATHEQUIV-PRIVATE/req-core-transport-002c-scoping>
